</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Carlson</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Measuring food security in the United States: household food security in the United States, 2002</article-title><source>Food Assistance and Nutrition Research Report Number 25 Washington, DC</source><year>2003</year></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Usfar</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Fahmida</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Februhartanty</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Household food security status measured by the US-Household Food Security/Hunger Survey Module [US-FSSM] is in line with coping strategy indicators found in urban and rural Indonesia</article-title><source>Asia Pac J Clin Nutr</source><year>2007</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>368</fpage><lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17468096</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rose</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Economic determinants and dietary consequences of food insecurity in the United States</article-title><source>J Nutr</source><year>1999</year><volume>129</volume><fpage>517S</fpage><lpage>20S</lpage><comment>Review</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10064321</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Opsomer</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Jensen</surname><given-names>HH</given-names></name><name><surname>Pan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An evaluation of the U.S. Department of Agriculture food security measure with generalized linear mixed models</article-title><source>J Nutr</source